    +ac._http_dict = lambda url, need, timeout=30, strict=False: fake(url)   # _go_module reads through _http_dict, so this keeps the case offline
  (hunk @@ -4415,5 +4415,5 @@ of .github/agent/tests/pin-age-check-test.sh; new line 4417; one commit f7454a53, parent 5cde60c7, no merge)
  Checker (.github/agent/supply-chain/pin-age-check.py, identical at base and head): _http_dict(url, need, timeout=30, strict=False)
  at line 233 calls _fetch_json (214, urlopen at 219); _http_json_strict at 242 returns _http_dict(..., strict=True);
  _http_json does not exist in the checker; _go_module at 323, line 328: info = _http_json_strict(url, _MODINFO) if strict else
  _http_dict(url, _MODINFO).
What the PR is: the Go-proxy case in pin-age-check-test.sh (about line 4407) stubbed `_http_json`, but the checker's
`_go_module` calls `_http_dict`. So the stub was never used and the case reached the real network: red offline, green in CI.
The PR changes the stub so that it replaces the function the checker really calls. Report each finding with file:line,
severity and whether it is a security finding; say "green" if none.
1. Right target: the stub now replaces the function `_go_module` calls, under the name the checker looks up at call time
   (module attribute or import, say which). It returns the shape `_http_dict` returns, so the code under test runs its real path
   and does not fail or pass on a shape mismatch.
2. Offline: with the stub in place, nothing in the case reaches the network. A seat with a shell runs pin-age-check-test.sh with
   no network in its sandbox at base and at head, and quotes both counts and the Go-proxy case's result.
3. Still proves its claim ("item 6: the Go proxy gets the !x case escaping ..."). The case must fail when the escaping is wrong.
   A seat with a shell breaks the escaping in a scratch copy of the checker and shows the case going red, then reverts. A case
   that passes either way is a finding.
4. Scope: one line, inside the Go-proxy case. No other case, no line of the vendored-folder guard or its lists, no checker file.
5. Other stubs: does any other case in the file stub `_http_json` where the checker calls `_http_dict` (the same fault)? Name
   each with file:line. They are outside this PR, so report them as notes, not findings against #780.
6. Simplest form (rules 1, 2, 8, 10): the fix is the smallest that works, adds no helper or layer, and keeps every line at 120
   characters or fewer.
7. Readability bar (owner Rule 16): a junior to mid-level developer must read the NEW line and understand it quickly. A line
   you cannot explain in one plain sentence is a finding.
8. Comments (owner Rule 17): a comment added that restates the code, or more comment than a competent human would write, is a
   finding. Comments say why, briefly.
End with one line: Verdict: GREEN or RED, then your numbered findings.

